    <string name="help_title">How to use</string>
    <string name="help_map_title">The map</string>
    <string name="help_map">Tap a road to see what it is, or a section to open its card. [location] centres the map on you and follows you. [menu] opens your routes and rides, your sections, the map region, this page and About.</string>
    <string name="help_plan_title">Plan a ride</string>
    <string name="help_plan">Long-press a place to start there, then long-press where you want to go; or [directions] route there from your position, or [loop] ride a loop from it. [loop] on the map plans loops from where you are. [share] sends a route or loop to your nav app as GPX; [save] keeps it under [menu] → Routes &amp; rides.</string>
    <string name="help_sections_title">Favourite roads</string>
    <string name="help_sections">[mark] marks a road you like: tap where it starts and where it ends, then rate it good, great or epic. Routes and loops lean towards your sections. [menu] → [sections] Sections lists them; pick one to see it, then [loop] loop through it or [directions] ride it from where you are.</string>
    <string name="help_ride_title">On a ride</string>
    <string name="help_ride">[record] records your ride. [tag] saves the spot you are on, to look at later; after the ride, [flag] shows how many spots wait for review, each one a road you may want to save as a section.</string>
    <string name="help_settings_title">Settings</string>
    <string name="help_settings">[settings] holds ride settings: gravel roads and the length new loops start at, the zooms of [location], and keeping the screen on while recording.</string>
